# Fourier Visualizer — draw a stroke; on release it is resampled, padded to a power of two, FFT'd into epicycles, and a chain of rotating circles redraws it over 20 s (Skia paths rebuilt in a UI-thread reaction).
# What this test covers: a diagonal stroke, the clear button while the epicycles run, a new stroke started while a
# previous reconstruction is mid-flight (onStart clears it), a long multi-segment-length stroke (thousands of FFT
# points), a two-finger pan, a full 20 s reconstruction until onComplete hides the clear button, and finally a
# very short stroke just past the pan slop (repro: a stroke that resamples to <= 1 point makes fft.js throw
# "FFT size must be a power of two and bigger than 1"; the LogBox is then dismissed).
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/fourier-visualizer"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 1000
# Diagonal stroke, let the epicycles run, then clear.
gesture pan 100 300 200 200 700
wait 2500
press 340 777
wait 800
# Start a new stroke while a reconstruction is running.
gesture pan 80 600 240 -150 600
wait 1500
gesture pan 320 250 -220 300 600
wait 2000
# Long stroke across the whole canvas (many FFT points).
gesture pan 30 180 340 600 1500
wait 2500
# Two-finger pan draws with the focal point.
gesture pan 150 500 100 -80 600 --pointer-count 2
wait 1500
# A medium stroke left to complete its full 20 s reconstruction (onComplete fades it and hides clear).
gesture pan 120 400 160 60 600
wait 21500
# Repro: a stroke barely past the pan activation slop.
gesture pan 200 600 12 0 300
wait 1500
press 110 816
wait 600
press 370 811
wait 600
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
